      ":question/problem": "$\\int \\frac{3 x^{2} - 4}{x^{3} - 4 x}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=x^{3} - 4 x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3 x^{2} - 4\\,\u27f9\\,\\text{d}u=(3 x^{2} - 4)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3 x^{2} - 4}{x^{3} - 4 x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x^{3} - 4 x}\\cdot (3 x^{2} - 4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}|u|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\\left|x^{3} - 4 x\\right|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
